module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.NodeQuadraticAlgebra.ConductorGlobal
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Derivation.ConductorGlobal
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Localization.CoatomAtMaximal

/-!
# The normalization of a nodal curve is generated by one element

Let `k` be a field, let `A` be a reduced Noetherian `k`-algebra and let
`A' = integralClosure A (FractionRing A)` be its normalization inside its total ring of
fractions. Suppose `𝔪₁, …, 𝔪ᵤ` are distinct maximal ideals accounting for all the singularities
of `A`: at each of them `A` is a nodal `k`-algebra, and at every other maximal ideal the local
ring is regular. Then there is a single `t ∈ A'` with

`A' = A[t]`,  `t² = a + c t`  for some `a, c ∈ A`.

This is item (1) of the data that
`Stacks.DerivationExtension.existsUnique_extend_integralClosure_apply_eq_zero_of_conductor`
consumes in order to extend a derivation of `A` to `A'`, and it is the item whose proof is
genuinely local-to-global.

The assembly has three inputs, all of them now available.

* The product of the nodes carries `A'` into `A`, by
  `Stacks.Curves.prod_smul_top_le_range_algebraMap_integralClosure_of_isNodalAlgebra`. This is
  the statement that the conductor cuts out the nodes.
* At each node the submodule `A + 𝔪ᵢ A'` is a coatom, which is proved here: its localization at
  `𝔪ᵢ` is the image of the local ring — the `𝔪ᵢ A'` summand disappears, being already inside
  that image — and coatomicity of a submodule containing `𝔪ᵢ A'` descends from a single
  localization by `Submodule.isCoatom_of_isCoatom_localized'`.
* Distinct maximal ideals are comaximal.

`Stacks.CyclicComaximal.exists_sup_span_singleton_eq_top_of_isCoatom_sup`, reached through
`Stacks.DerivationExtension.exists_adjoin_eq_integralClosure_of_isCoatom`, then glues the
generators at the separate nodes into one. The quadratic relation is free: `t² ∈ A' = A + A t`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Curves.isCoatom_range_algebraMap_integralClosure_sup_smul_top_of_isNodalAlgebra`: at a
  node `𝔪`, the submodule `A + 𝔪 A'` of `A'` is a coatom, so `A' / (A + 𝔪 A')` is simple.
* `Stacks.Curves.exists_adjoin_eq_integralClosure_of_isNodalAlgebra`: the normalization is
  generated over `A` by one element satisfying a monic quadratic relation.

## Implementation notes

The coatom statement is global — it is about submodules of `A'` over `A`, with no localization
in it — while its proof is the node-local computation
`Stacks.Curves.isCoatom_range_algebraMap_localization_integralClosure_of_isNodalAlgebra`. The
descent is legitimate for this particular submodule because `A + 𝔪 A'` contains `𝔪 A'`, which
pins down the quotient away from `𝔪`: there it vanishes. Coatomicity does *not* in general
descend from one maximal ideal, and no hypothesis here says anything about the other maximal
ideals of `A`.

The regularity hypothesis is therefore used only for the conductor statement, not for the coatom
statements, and the two are taken in the same dichotomous form as in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.NodeQuadraticAlgebra.ConductorGlobal`: quantified over the
maximal ideals of `A`, so that `Localization.AtPrime P` elaborates without the caller producing
a primality instance for each member of the family.

Distinctness of the `𝔪ᵢ` is assumed here, unlike in the conductor statement, because the Chinese
remainder step needs them comaximal.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E68](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E68)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1X)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open IsLocalRing

universe u v

namespace Stacks.Curves

/-- **At a node, the ring plus the maximal ideal times the normalization is a coatom.** Let `A`
be a reduced Noetherian algebra over a field `k`, let `A'` be its integral closure in its total
ring of fractions and let `𝔪` be a maximal ideal at which `A` is a nodal `k`-algebra. Then the
`A`-submodule `A + 𝔪 A'` of `A'` is a coatom, that is, `A' / (A + 𝔪 A')` is a simple
`A`-module.

Unlike its local counterpart
`Stacks.Curves.isCoatom_range_algebraMap_localization_integralClosure_of_isNodalAlgebra`, this
is a statement about the global `A'`, which is the form the Chinese remainder step over the
several nodes needs. The descent works because the submodule contains `𝔪 A'`, so the quotient is
a module over the residue field at `𝔪` and localizing at `𝔪` loses nothing; after localizing,
the summand `𝔪 A'` is absorbed into the image of the local ring, by the conductor computation at
the node. -/
public theorem isCoatom_range_algebraMap_integralClosure_sup_smul_top_of_isNodalAlgebra
    (k : Type u) (A : Type v) [Field k] [CommRing A] [IsReduced A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [Algebra k A] (𝔪 : Ideal A) [𝔪.IsMaximal]
    (hnodal : IsNodalAlgebra k (Localization.AtPrime 𝔪)) :
    IsCoatom (LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A))) ⊔
      𝔪 • (⊤ : Submodule A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)))) := by
  refine Submodule.isCoatom_of_isCoatom_localized' 𝔪
    (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A))
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid
        ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) 𝔪.primeCompl))).toLinearMap
    (Localization.AtPrime 𝔪) le_sup_right ?_
  rw [Submodule.localized'_sup_smul_top_range_algebraLinearMap,
    Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal,
    sup_eq_left.mpr (by
      rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_map]
      exact fun t ht => map_maximalIdeal_le_range_algebraMap_localization_integralClosure
        k A 𝔪 hnodal t ht)]
  exact isCoatom_range_algebraMap_localization_integralClosure_of_isNodalAlgebra k A 𝔪 hnodal

/-- **The normalization of a nodal curve is monogenic over it.** Let `A` be a reduced Noetherian
algebra over a field `k` whose singularities are a finite family of distinct maximal ideals
`𝔪ᵢ`, each a node, and let `A'` be the integral closure of `A` in its total ring of fractions.
Then `A' = A[t]` for a single `t`, and `t` satisfies a monic quadratic relation
`t² = a + c t` over `A`. -/
public theorem exists_adjoin_eq_integralClosure_of_isNodalAlgebra
    (k : Type u) (A : Type v) [Field k] [CommRing A] [IsReduced A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [Algebra k A] {ι : Type*} (𝔪 : ι → Ideal A) (s : Finset ι)
    (hmax : ∀ i ∈ s, (𝔪 i).IsMaximal)
    (hdistinct : ∀ i ∈ s, ∀ j ∈ s, i ≠ j → 𝔪 i ≠ 𝔪 j)
    (hnodal : ∀ (P : Ideal A) [P.IsMaximal], (∃ i ∈ s, 𝔪 i = P) →
      IsNodalAlgebra k (Localization.AtPrime P))
    (hreg : ∀ (P : Ideal A) [P.IsMaximal], (∀ i ∈ s, 𝔪 i ≠ P) →
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime P)) :
    ∃ (t : ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A))) (a c : A),
      Algebra.adjoin A ({(t : FractionRing A)} : Set (FractionRing A)) =
          integralClosure A (FractionRing A) ∧
        t * t = algebraMap A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) a +
          algebraMap A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) c * t :=
  Stacks.DerivationExtension.exists_adjoin_eq_integralClosure_of_isCoatom 𝔪 s
    (fun i hi j hj hij => (hmax i hi).coprime_of_ne (hmax j hj) (hdistinct i hi j hj hij))
    (prod_smul_top_le_range_algebraMap_integralClosure_of_isNodalAlgebra k A 𝔪 s hnodal hreg)
    fun i hi =>
      have := hmax i hi
      isCoatom_range_algebraMap_integralClosure_sup_smul_top_of_isNodalAlgebra k A (𝔪 i)
        (hnodal (𝔪 i) ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩)

end Stacks.Curves

end
